WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:01.750
Hey Thoughty2 here.

00:00:01.750 --> 00:00:04.500
How would you dispose of a body?

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:07.390
There are countless ways, or so I’ve been
told.

00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:13.460
But one 20th century Italian woman had a method
of disposing of bodies that even Mrs Lovett

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:16.510
and her pies would have been disgusted by.

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:23.390
Serial killer Leonarda Cianciulli turned her
victims into bars of soap and teacakes, and

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:28.510
that’s not even the worst bit, but before
we get into that, let’s learn a little about

00:00:28.510 --> 00:00:32.189
what drove her to murder in the first place.

00:00:32.189 --> 00:00:36.520
Psychologists have long believed that an unsteady
upbringing can contribute to one becoming

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:38.399
a psychotic murderer.

00:00:38.399 --> 00:00:42.630
Both Stalin and Hitler, had a highly dysfunctional
childhood.

00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:49.390
Leonarda Cianciulli is no exception to this
rule, she was born out of rape in 1894 in

00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:50.730
Montella, Italy.

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:55.250
Her mother never wanted her, yet was left
with no choice but to raise her.

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:58.930
Safe to say, Leonarda had a rather dysfunctional
upbringing.

00:00:58.930 --> 00:01:04.509
At the age of 23 Leonarda defiantly married
a local registry clerk, against the wishes

00:01:04.509 --> 00:01:05.979
of her parents.

00:01:05.979 --> 00:01:10.459
Her mother was so upset that she “cursed”
the newly-weds.

00:01:10.459 --> 00:01:15.770
Leonarda had always been highly superstitious
and paranoid, so she took a lot of offence

00:01:15.770 --> 00:01:17.009
to the curse.

00:01:17.009 --> 00:01:19.700
Things quickly got worse from here.

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:28.850
Leonarda, got pregnant 17 times, three were
lost to miscarriges, and 10 others died when

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:30.240
they were very young.

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:37.409
Who knows whether this was a series of extremely
unlucky coincidences, or had she really succumb

00:01:37.409 --> 00:01:40.399
to the evil ways of her mother’s curse?

00:01:40.399 --> 00:01:46.029
Needless to say Leonarda became ultra protective
over her four remaining children.

00:01:46.029 --> 00:01:50.789
She sought help by visiting a fortune teller,
who decided that this poor women’s life

00:01:50.789 --> 00:01:55.739
wasn’t already tragic enough and told her
that she would either end up in prison or

00:01:55.739 --> 00:01:57.479
a criminal asylum.

00:01:57.479 --> 00:02:01.709
Despite being an ultra-paranoid potential
psychopath on the brink of a mental breakdown,

00:02:01.709 --> 00:02:06.619
all was going well for a while for Leonarda
and her four children.

00:02:06.619 --> 00:02:12.860
Until one of their lives came under threat;
in 1939 her eldest son decided to fight for

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:15.670
the Italian army in World War II.

00:02:15.670 --> 00:02:20.799
Leonarda didn’t like this and couldn’t
bare the thought of losing another child,

00:02:20.799 --> 00:02:23.470
so she came up with a genius plan.

00:02:23.470 --> 00:02:29.329
She concluded that if she found another human
sacrifice, they would then take her son’s

00:02:29.329 --> 00:02:36.270
place in the afterlife, and so her son would
somehow be supernaturally protected from death.

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:40.569
And so she set out to find her first victim.

00:02:40.569 --> 00:02:45.939
Leonarda was actually an amateur fortune teller
herself, she often practiced on the local

00:02:45.939 --> 00:02:47.290
women in her village.

00:02:47.290 --> 00:02:52.390
I’m not sure how you practice fortune telling,
presumably you just keep makes guesses until

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:54.010
you get something right.

00:02:54.010 --> 00:03:00.480
She chose her first victim carefully, Faustina
Setti was a client of Lenoardas.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:06.370
During one session Leonarda told a depressed
and hopeless Faustina that she would find

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:12.340
the husband of her dreams and her life would
be all rosy, if she leaves and travels to

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:13.940
a neighbouring town.

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:19.209
She also cleverly instructed Faustina that
she must immediately write letters to all

00:03:19.209 --> 00:03:24.680
her friends and family informing them that
she intends to travel to another town to find

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:25.909
a husband.

00:03:25.909 --> 00:03:30.370
And so Leonarda thought she had created the
groundwork for the perfect murder.

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:35.260
Faustina visited Leonarda one last time before
she left town.

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:41.079
Leonarda poured two glasses of wine as a toast
to Faustina’s new life.

00:03:41.079 --> 00:03:46.959
Of course, Faustina’s wine was drugged with
sedatives.

00:03:46.959 --> 00:03:53.420
After she was out cold, Leonarda bludgeoned
her helpless victim to death with an axe.

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:58.760
And so began Leonarda’s twisted method of
disposing of the corpse.

00:03:58.760 --> 00:04:04.170
First she chopped the corpse into 9 equal-sized
pieces, to make it more manageable.

00:04:04.170 --> 00:04:09.450
She drained the blood then put the dried pieces
into a giant pot along with caustic soda,

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:12.790
a primary ingredient in soap-making.

00:04:12.790 --> 00:04:18.079
And yes, she then turned the corpse bits into
bars of soap.

00:04:18.079 --> 00:04:23.870
Which seems almost comical when you learn
what she did with the blood from the body.

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:30.160
Leonarda dried the blood in an oven, mixed
it with eggs, flour, sugar, milk, chocolate

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:34.840
and margarine, because you know, if you’re
going to make delicacies out of dead humans

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:37.740
then at least have the decency to make them
low fat.

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:41.430
She then baked the sickening mixture into
Italian teacakes.

00:04:41.430 --> 00:04:45.090
She then shared the teacakes around her neighbours.

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:49.819
Even more disturbingly, Leonarda and her son
ate them up also.

00:04:49.819 --> 00:04:56.680
Leonarda went on to carry out the same murderous
process on two more of her female fortune-telling

00:04:56.680 --> 00:04:57.740
clients.

00:04:57.740 --> 00:05:01.569
Her final victim was a local soprano called
Virginia Cacioppo.

00:05:01.569 --> 00:05:07.320
Leonarda later wrote in her memoirs that she
had flesh that was “fat and white” and

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:12.400
apparently she made “a most acceptable creamy
soap”.

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:19.050
Also Leonarda noted that Cacioppo made the
best teacakes so far quoting “that woman

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:20.240
was really sweet.”

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:26.410
The words don’t even exist to describe how
disturbed this woman truly was.

00:05:26.410 --> 00:05:31.690
But that sweet taste wouldn’t last long
because the sister of Leonarda’s final victim

00:05:31.690 --> 00:05:36.630
grew suspicious of her disappearance and she
informed the police that she had last seen

00:05:36.630 --> 00:05:42.260
her sister, Virginia Cacioppo, entering the
home of Leonarda Cianciulli.

00:05:42.260 --> 00:05:48.520
Leonarda was swiftly arrested and she confessed
to all her messed-up soapy, tea cake murders.

00:05:48.520 --> 00:05:53.960
She was sentenced to 30 years in prison and
three years in a criminal asylum for the mentally

00:05:53.960 --> 00:06:03.970
ill – just as the fortune teller had predicted
all those years ago.

00:06:03.970 --> 00:06:19.449
Thanks for watching.

